### The void binary — see void/cli (SPEC.md §5.17, ROADMAP 1.6).
###
### A thin launcher. An application pins its own void with
### `jpm --local deps`; this finds it. The syspath swap has to happen
### *before* (import void/cli): swap it after and the CLI itself stays
### the one from the global tree while the application's void/http comes
### from the local one — two copies of void/core in one process
### (ADR-0020).
###
### No shebang here: jpm writes it on install (:is-janet true), and a
### second one would end up in the installed file verbatim.

(when (= :directory (os/stat "jpm_tree/lib" :mode))
  (put root-env :syspath (string (os/cwd) "/jpm_tree/lib")))

(import void/cli :as cli)

(defn main [& args]
  (cli/main ;args))
